      "content": "It's crucial not to double up on your medication, as this can be dangerous. However, given your throat feels tight and it's hard to swallow, you should seek medical attention right away to ensure it's not a serious allergic reaction worsening. Call a pharmacy to get an antihistamine like cetirizine from a nurse for temporary relief while you arrange to see a doctor. It's better to be safe and address these symptoms professionally.",
