      "content": "I understand your frustration with the inconvenience of emergency rooms, but difficulty swallowing, especially with a sensation of tightness, can be indicative of a more serious condition, such as anaphylaxis. It's essential to avoid doubling your medication. Take one of your allergy medications as advised on the label, and take an antihistamine like cetirizine that can be obtained over the counter at your pharmacy. Then, wait for another 30 minutes to see if there’s any improvement; if your symptoms persist or worsen, or if you start experiencing facial swelling, difficulty breathing, or a drop in blood pressure, call emergency services immediately. Your safety is vital. It's better to be proactive with your symptoms than to risk ignoring them.",
